.SH "نام (NAME)"
lr_log2mail \- send a report generated from a log file by email
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBlr_log2mail\fR \fB[\fR\f(BIoptions\fR\fB]\fR \fIservice\fR \fIaddresses\fR...
.PP
\&\fBlr_log2report\fR \fB\-\-version\fR
.PP
\&\fBlr_log2report\fR \fB\-\-help\fR \fB[dlf\-converters|output\-formats|report\-templates]\fR
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP "\fB\-\-help\fR \fB[\fR\fIsection\fR\fB]\fR" 4
.IX Item "--help [section]"
If no argument is given, prints usage information and exits. Argument
can be one of the following:
.RS 4
.IP dlf\-converters 4
.IX Item "dlf-converters"
Prints the list of available DLF converters and exits.
.IP output\-formats 4
.IX Item "output-formats"
Prints the list of available output formats and exits.
.IP report\-templates 4
.IX Item "report-templates"
Prints the list of available report templates and exits.
.RE
.RS 4
.RE
.IP \fB\-\-version\fR 4
.IX Item "--version"
Prints Lire\*(Aqs version and exits.
.IP "\fB\-\-output\-format|\-o\fR \fIoutput format\fR" 4
.IX Item "--output-format|-o output format"
Selects the ouput format in which to generate the report.
.IP "\fB\-\-template\fR \fIname\fR" 4
.IX Item "--template name"
Uses the report configuration named \fIname\fR to generate the report.
.IP "\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fIlogfile\fR" 4
.IX Item "--log-file logfile"
Selects the log file that should be processed instead of STDIN.
.IP "\fB\-\-subject|\-s\fR \fIsubject\fR" 4
.IX Item "--subject|-s subject"
Sets the subject of the email message. Defaults to \*(AqYour \fIformat\fR report\*(Aq.
.IP "\fB\-\-extra\-file\fR \fIfile\fR" 4
.IX Item "--extra-file file"
An additional text file that will be sent along the report. If the
output format is txt, it will be appended to the report.
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The \fBlr_log2mail\fR command is similar to the \fBlr_log2report\fR\|(1) command
with the difference that the report is sent by email. The log file is
read from STDIN or from the file specified using the \fB\-\-log\-file\fR
option. The format of the log file is specified using the
\&\fIdlf_converter\fR argument. Use the \fB\-\-help\-dlf\-converters\fR option to
get a list of all currently available DLF converters. All remaining
arguments are interpreted as email addresses to which to send the
report. In case the log is passed in a compressed format, it\*(Aqs
uncompressed on the fly, using \fBgzip\fR\|(1).
.PP
The report will be encapsulated in a MIME email appropriate for the
output format. For example, ASCII reports will be sent inline, PDF
reports will be sent as a file attachment and HTML reports should
appear inline in a HTML\-capable mail reader.
.PP
The From and Reply\-To headers in the outgoing emails are set to the
values of the \fIlr_mail_from\fR and \fIlr_mail_replyto\fR configuration
variables.
.SH "مثال (EXAMPLE)"
.IX Header "EXAMPLE"
.Vb 2
\& % lr_log2mail \-s "bind8 report" bind8_query \e
\&     root "Joe User <joe@example.com>" < /var/log/query.log
.Ve
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBlr_log2report\fR\|(1), \fBlr_xml2report\fR\|(1), \fBlr_xml2mail\fR\|(1), \fBlire\fR\|(1), \fBlire\fR\|(7),
documentation in the Lire User Manual
